## Activity 2: Image Compression - K-Means Color Quantization

### Compression Process
```
Original Image          →        Reshape        →    K-Means Clustering    →   Reconstruct
(Height × Width × 3)        (N_pixels × 3 RGB)        (Find k colors)          Compressed Image
    ~24M colors                    ↓                         ↓                     (k colors)
                                Pixel data              Cluster centers         ~4-32 colors
```

### Color Quantization Results

| k (Colors) | Bits per pixel | Compression Ratio | Image Quality |
|------------|----------------|-------------------|---------------|
| 4 | 2 bits | ~12:1 | Posterized, noticeable banding |
| 8 | 3 bits | ~8:1 | Blocky, but recognizable |
| 16 | 4 bits | ~6:1 | Good quality, slight banding |
| 32 | 5 bits | ~4.8:1 | Near-original quality |

